   "text": "This SMILES was written from the drawing by reading it in sections; I did not run it through a parser. Four things in it rest on assumption or recollection rather than being read from the image.\n\n- **Overall structure:** a central tertiary amide nitrogen carries two identical arms and an acyl group.\n  - The acyl group is the maleimide-terminated linker, C(=O)CH2OCH2CH2OCH2CH2\u2013N-maleimide.\n  - Each arm runs N\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013(1,4-disubstituted 1,2,3-triazole)\u2013CH2CH2(OCH2CH2)2O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2\u2013 into the 2-position of a benzoselenophene.\n- **Benzoselenophene:** it carries a \u03b2-D-glucuronic acid O-linked at C4 and a CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(Me) carbamate at C7.\n- **Payload:** the carbamate nitrogen is the N-methyl-valine end of an MMAE-type chain. The chain runs N-Me-Val, Val, N-Me-dolaisoleucine (with OMe), dolaproine (with OMe) and the norephedrine unit.\n- **Stereochemistry assumptions:**\n  - I took the payload stereochemistry from my recollection of the MMAE SMILES and re-derived it for the reversed writing order, rather than checking every centre against the wedges.\n  - I assumed the bottom arm is the top arm flipped over in 3D, which would explain wedges becoming hashes, so both arms get identical stereo.\n  - I took the glucuronide as \u03b2-D, with the centres derived from the \u03b2-D-glucose SMILES by permutation.\n\nSMILES: O=C(COCCOCCN1C(=O)C=CC1=O)N(CCOCc3cn(CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CCc4cc5c(O[C@@H]6O[C@H](C(=O)O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]6O)ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1[C@@H]([C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)[C@H](c2ccccc2)O)OC)c5[se]4)nn3)CCOCc3cn(CCOCCOCCOCCNC(=O)CCc4cc5c(O[C@@H]6O[C@H](C(=O)O)[C@@H](O)[C@H](O)[C@H]6O)ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1[C@@H]([C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)[C@H](c2ccccc2)O)OC)c5[se]4)nn3"
